    "created_at": "2017-11-28T08:58:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-11-28T08:58:29Z",
    "body": "The spec doesn't say so, but I believe the order should be the same as if the resource loaded one byte at a time, so that at the very least changing readyState of HAVE_METADATA happens after the audio and video tracks have been added.\r\n\r\nWhat's not at all obvious, though, is whether all audio tracks should be announced before all video tracks, or if this should just depend on the order they exist in the container. Testing existing implementations would be a good idea, and it looks like Edge and Safari have these APIs.\r\n\r\n@mounirlamouri @wolenetz, do you either of you plan to work on audio/video tracks? Thoughts on this issue?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
